[TEST_CASE]
UID: TC-H1FWHVPS-36
TITLE: External ADC invalid-result handling - Test Case
STATEMENT: >>>
The firmware shall reject external ADC results containing framing, DMA, or
acquisition-timing errors and shall not use an invalid result for feedback
processing.
<<<
PREREQUISITES: >>>
* The system is powered on and operating with valid external ADC feedback.
* A bus or firmware fault-injection method is available.
* Feedback result status or equivalent diagnostic logging is available.
<<<
STEPS: >>>
1. Capture a valid external ADC result.
2. Inject an invalid ADC framing condition.
3. Repeat with an ADC DMA-transfer error.
4. Delay or suppress ADC completion so a complete result is not available within 2 ms.
5. Observe the result status and feedback-control outputs.
6. Restore valid ADC communication and capture the next result.
<<<
EXPECTED_BEHAVIOR: >>>
1. Verify the valid result is accepted.
2. Verify the framing error is reported as invalid.
3. Verify the DMA error is reported as invalid.
4. Verify the burst is reported as invalid when a complete result is not available within 2 ms.
5. Verify invalid feedback is not used for feedback processing or output control.
6. Verify valid feedback processing resumes after communication is restored.
<<<
